  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between 8-O-(3-Hydroxy-3-Methylbutyryl)Desacylcynaropicrin and HEp-2 cells, mediated through a splicing factor, proline- and glutamine-rich, which is targeted by both the compound and oxybenzone. This indicates that the compound may act as a competitive inhibitor of the splicing factor, potentially affecting RNA processing in HEp-2 cells. The presence of multiple pathways converging on the splicing factor, proline- and glutamine-rich, supports the idea that the compound may influence cellular processes through this intermediate. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which the compound interacts with HEp-2 cells, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
